# Smoke-tier SID corpus. 7 SIDs hand-picked to exercise every macro
# class the encoder produces, end-to-end wallclock target < 10 min per
# experiment arm with a warm dump cache.
#
# Coverage rubric (one line per class):
#   BACK_REF / PATTERN_REPLAY     LoopPass + transposed/fuzzy variants
#   GATE_REPLAY palette           GateMacroPass; bundle replay
#   PLAY_INSTRUMENT body          InstrumentProgramPass; envelope replay
#   INTERVAL mirror               IntervalPass; cross-voice freq link
#   PWM / FilterSweep burst       PwmPass / FilterSweepPass
#   Long DELAY frames             Variable-IRQ idle handling
#   PAL + NTSC                    irq mapping divergence
#
# Path format: ``<HVSC_VERSION>``-relative, ``MUSICIANS/<L>/<Composer>/<song>.<tune>.dump.parquet``.
# The list is read by ``integration_tests/experiments/base.py`` which
# resolves each entry against ``--hvsc-root`` (default
# ``/scratch/preframr/training-dumps``).
#
# Edit policy: this list is pinned. Re-curation is a deliberate event
# (record the rationale in the commit message); single-arm experiments
# that care about specific data should reference this file unmodified.
MUSICIANS/G/Goto80/Truth.1.dump.parquet                # short, dense, voice-rotated
MUSICIANS/G/Goto80/Acid_10000.1.dump.parquet           # GATE_REPLAY-rich
MUSICIANS/G/Goto80/Skybox.1.dump.parquet               # InstrumentProgramPass
MUSICIANS/G/Goto80/CBM_85.1.dump.parquet               # PATTERN_REPLAY-rich
MUSICIANS/H/Hubbard_Rob/Commando.1.dump.parquet        # long ADSR (long-form PI)
MUSICIANS/G/Galway_Martin/Yie_Ar_Kung_Fu.1.dump.parquet  # arpeggio (xframe TRANSPOSE)
MUSICIANS/T/Tel_Jeroen/Afterburner.1.dump.parquet      # NTSC bias
